@startuml
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.7 “Approve or Reject Vessel Visit Notification”

actor "Port Authority Officer" as Officer
boundary "VesselVisitNotificationController\n(API Layer)" as Controller
control "VesselVisitNotificationService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "VesselVisitNotificationRepository\n(Domain/Infrastructure)" as Repository
database "PortManagementContext (EF Core)\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

note over Officer
User Story 2.2.7 – Approve or Reject Vessel Visit Notifications

"As a Port Authority Officer, I want to approve or reject
submitted vessel visit notifications, so that port operations
are controlled and scheduled properly."
end note

== Approve Vessel Visit ==

Officer -> Controller : PUT /api/vesselvisitnotification/{id}/approve\n?officerId=&dockId=
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : ApproveAsync(id, officerId, dockId)
activate Service

Service -> Repository : GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : SELECT * FROM VesselVisitNotifications WHERE Id = id
activate DB
DB --> Repository : VesselVisitNotification (Status = Submitted)
deactivate DB
Repository --> Service : VesselVisitNotification
deactivate Repository

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Visit must be in "Submitted" status.
- Dock must be available.
- Officer ID must be valid.
end note

Service -> Service : visit.Approve(officerId, dockId)
Service -> Repository : UpdateAsync(visit)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : UPDATE VesselVisitNotifications SET Status='Approved', DockId=dockId
DB --> Repository : OK
deactivate Repository
Service --> Controller : Success
deactivate Service

Controller --> Officer : 204 No Content
deactivate Controller

== Reject Vessel Visit ==

Officer -> Controller : PUT /api/vesselvisitnotification/{id}/reject\nBody: reason
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : RejectAsync(id, officerId, reason)
activate Service

Service -> Repository : GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : SELECT * FROM VesselVisitNotifications WHERE Id = id
DB --> Repository : VesselVisitNotification (Status = Submitted)
Repository --> Service : VesselVisitNotification
deactivate Repository

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Rejection allowed only for "Submitted" visits.
- Officer must provide a reason.
- Rejected visits remain visible in history.
end note

Service -> Service : visit.Reject(officerId, reason)
Service -> Repository : UpdateAsync(visit)
Repository -> DB : UPDATE VesselVisitNotifications SET Status='Rejected'
DB --> Repository : OK
Repository --> Service : Confirmation
Service --> Controller : Success
deactivate Service

Controller --> Officer : 204 No Content
deactivate Controller
@enduml
